// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 9 (Impl-N): divergence class 1 made
// executable — counting-through-recursion, the E-ZADM rejection.
//
// The body r(a) :- r(a) with seed 1 (generalized: r(a) += incr every
// round) is MONOTONE but diverges: the per-key carrier is ℤ, an
// INFINITE-HEIGHT lattice, so the convergence theorem's premise fails
// — monotone ≠ finite-height, BOTH are required (W2C §3.3's first
// named divergence class). The bracket would never quiesce: every
// round's delta re-derives a strictly larger count.
//
// `zfix_count` is the surface's counting-through-recursion mode: a
// RECOGNIZED intrinsic (a named, checked diagnostic — not "unknown
// function") that the checker ALWAYS rejects with E-ZADM. Admission
// is undecidable in general; the checker is the sufficient condition
// priced at expressiveness, and refusals are compile-time errors,
// never silent divergence (W2C §3.5). This file is a compile-FAIL
// golden case (tests/golden.rs).

fn main() {
    ptr seed = zset_new(0)
    zset_add(seed, 1, 1)
    zfix_count(seed, 1) // must be rejected: E-ZADM
}
